 Invalid operation objects, invalid JSON Pointers, unresolvable paths (including removal of the document root), and failed `test` operations throw an error. Operations are evaluated in order and stop at the first error; the supplied document is never changed.
 
+## Creating JSON Patches
+
+`createPatch(from, to)` creates an [RFC 6902 JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902) that transforms one JSON document into another. It emits targeted member and array edits where possible, so a small nested change does not require transmitting the whole document. Neither input is mutated.
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+const patch = createPatch(
+  { service: { retries: 2, enabled: true } },
+  { service: { retries: 3, enabled: true } },
+); // [{ op: "replace", path: "/service/retries", value: 3 }]
+```
+
 ## JSON Merge Patch
 
 `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies an [RFC 7386 JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386)
